cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this kernel in academic or industrial work, please cite it
  using the metadata below.
title: "zero-point-kernel"
abstract: >-
  A small x86-64 research kernel written in Rust, no_std, that boots under
  QEMU and on real hardware, and that runs every state-changing request
  past a policy gate before carrying it out. Each decision is appended to
  a linked log, which detects accidental corruption but is not
  tamper-evident against a writer. The private policy engine is not
  included; a demo policy is, so a build from this source runs and the
  gate can be observed working. Contains the kernel (`zpl-kernel`), its
  bare-metal binary (`zpl-kernel-bin`), a Limine bridge for booting from
  an ISO (`limine-bridge`), a small assembler (`zpl-asm`), a filesystem
  format and image tool (`zpl-fs` + `zpl-mkfs`), a log replay tool
  (`audit-replay`), and a QEMU test runner (`zpl-test-runner`).
type: software
